{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras","id":878180,"title":"[2E] Left Hand Yantras","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-29T15:39:15-07:00","id":878180,"title":"[2E] Left Hand Yantras","content":"<span style=\"font-size:9px\"><i>( <b>N</b><b>ote:</b> Yes, I know it's only days before premiere. But this idea springs to me on and off few months now, so I lay ground work for the talk about it. If you do not want to discuss before proper corebook, return just in one week time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</i></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">We know them all. Sacrificing virgin. Still beating heart ripped from chest. Blood of the new born. Shattering innocent.</span></i><br /> <br /> Fiction about evil sorcerers and using morally black &quot;components&quot; is full of them. I assume we will not see them in corebook as those examples are extreme - but they are needed for truly Black Arts magicians stories. Our Scelesti and Mad need this kind of roads to power. Need to uncover them in damned Grimoires of Left Hand mages. You get the drill.<br /> <br /> <b>So how they should work?</b> Well, we talk here about extreme stuff that most people would not like to get into, even Awakened. So it should have real power to make them tempted. But also heavy price on Wisdom of user. Relating this to <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-lever-and-a-firm-place-to-stand/\" target=\"_blank\">Yantras rules spoiler</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yantras spoiler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unlocking the Imago</b> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">When a mage uses a Yantra in the working of a spell, she adds bonus dice to her spellcasting dice pool. The number of dice varies by the Yantra that she uses. These bonus dice can help eliminate penalties to her spellcasting pool, or provide bonuses. A mage can only get so much help from Yantras \u2014 after offsetting any penalties, the maximum bonus from all her Yantras combined cannot exceed 5 dice.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A mage may want to use as many Yantras as possible in her spellcasting, especially for powerful acts of magic. She can however only access so many pieces of Supernal knowledge at once. To reflect this, the number of Yantras she can apply to a given spellcasting pool is limited by her Gnosis. If she uses one ritual item in many ways, each individual use counts as one Yantra for this limit.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Listed Yantras gives up to +3 bonus each, in maximum positive example. <b>To beat it, t</b><b>he truly Black Arts stuff should give you an extreme +5 for each Yantra - but it's Wisdom sin to use them.</b> Not even just because they are immoral - but because you do really hardcore actions to fuel your magic, shattering your own sense of limits - what is definition of Unwise behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-29-2016, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:23:01-07:00","id":878219,"title":"","content":"I've always been more inclined to treat the lure of &quot;powerful sacrifices&quot; (lives and souls mostly) as sort of pre-Archmastery quintessences that allow the normal restrictions on certain magic to be broken (like allowing effects otherwise temporary to become permanent). The &quot;reach&quot; rules may end up superceding this though. We'll see on Wednesday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:35:18-07:00","id":878225,"title":"","content":"Can you be a haruspex that uses human organs for your Fate spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T17:16:26-07:00","id":878253,"title":"","content":"Aw. I thought you were going to be referencing something like the Ozaki Eight.<br /> <br /> I think you can get at what you want by saying certain yantras give you 1 additional Reach. The drawback of doing so is that, since the criteria for the yantra is very exact, you have to get it perfect or you'll gain nothing and instead have an additional Paradox dice. Or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T18:48:46-07:00","id":878323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878225#post878225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you be a haruspex that uses human organs for your Fate spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not see a problem on that with Yantras way - haruspicy ( or any other common occult practice ) then is just &quot;focusing&quot; Awakened Supernal Magic. As those practices are much more known to mage even before his Awakening, they resonate him harder and make clearer Imago for his spells. This sacrificing or harming humans have a &quot;boost&quot; of also shattering moral limitation of mage, so his Magic is much less restrained that for normal Awakened.<br /> <br /> I would say that haruspicy of animals give +1 bonus for animals to each up Size 5, up to +3 for animals of Size 15 ( Taking down elephant is really extreme ) - IF animal symbology fit with prediction of both Time and Fate. On the other hand - humans organs would always gives you +5, for &quot;shattering limits of what human should to another&quot;, but risking Wisdom degeneration.<br /> <br /> Still, need to asses those with corebook rules and bonuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878253#post878253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aw. I thought you were going to be referencing something like the Ozaki Eight.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does &quot;father of the Japanese Constitution&quot; have in common with magical focusing practices / using exotic components ( i.e. Yantras system )?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878253#post878253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you can get at what you want by saying certain yantras give you 1 additional Reach. The drawback of doing so is that, since the criteria for the yantra is very exact, you have to get it perfect or you'll gain nothing and instead have an additional Paradox dice. Or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that 1 additional Reach can be to low on this - it's easily to take 1 Paradox dice and get the same result. Especially, as those practices would mostly be Wisdom sins - then no player would not play with them. <br /> <br /> Maybe 3 extra Reach will do fine, but do not sure how this imbalance system. We will see - I will have this idea in mind when looking over rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:07:25-07:00","id":878375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878225#post878225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you be a haruspex that uses human organs for your Fate spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's even a legacy for that, though I think the ruling arcana is Time instead of Fate.<br /> <br /> The two most common Yantras that give a +2 are High Speech and Rote Mudras. I don't really see a need for &quot;extreme&quot; Yantras to give more than a +3. I mean, a virgin sacrifice has got to be easier to come by than say a unicorn horn and that would only give a +3 at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-29-2016, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:27:44-07:00","id":878388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878323#post878323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does &quot;father of the Japanese Constitution&quot; have in common with magical focusing practices / using exotic components ( i.e. Yantras system )?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_Break_(2015_film)#Plot\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_...015_film)#Plot</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">According to the movie character Johnny Utah 'the Osaki 8' is named after Ono Osaki, an eco-warrior who challenged the extreme sports world to a series of eight ordeals that honor the forces of nature. The challenge is to create a perfect line when completing the trials. Although Johnny Utah claims it is a path to enlightenment, Bodhi says that Ono Osaki was more interested in balance than enlightenment and he and the others in his group appear to want to use the teaching for liberating rather than material gain, even though it involves criminal activity.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Osaki 8 include:</span></span></span><ul><li>Emerging Force</li> <li>Birth of Sky</li> <li>Awakening Earth</li> <li>Life of Water</li> <li>Life of Wind</li> <li>Life of Ice</li> <li>Master of Six Lives</li> <li>Act of Ultimate Trust</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>I went and saw this movie after the Mysterium discussions we had on this forum. I hoped it would help me think about them. /shrug<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878323#post878323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that 1 additional Reach can be to low on this - it's easily to take 1 Paradox dice and get the same result. Especially, as those practices would mostly be Wisdom sins - then no player would not play with them.<br /> <br /> Maybe 3 extra Reach will do fine, but do not sure how this imbalance system. We will see - I will have this idea in mind when looking over rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I'm not saying my suggestion is finely honed or anything, especially before seeing the final rules. I'm just throwing out an idea for others to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":2758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","user":"Errol216","date":". 04-29-2016, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:20:09-07:00","id":878463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878375#post878375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two most common Yantras that give a +2 are High Speech and Rote Mudras. I don't really see a need for &quot;extreme&quot; Yantras to give more than a +3. I mean, a virgin sacrifice has got to be easier to come by than say a unicorn horn and that would only give a +3 at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but we almost all assume it those &quot;dark Yantras&quot; will be Wisdom sins. As player, I would avoid at any cost using this kind Yantra if it would only by +1 bonus better than typical normal ones - <i>convenience</i> here is not enough to shatter characters Wisdom and go whole Left Hand Path on this. You do not go whole Black Magic path, if you can easily have the same mechanical effect with out it.<br /> <br /> Remember, character on spellcasting still can use Willpower points, so they get &quot;free&quot; +3 to roll. If you only need &quot;want it hard enough&quot; to get free +3, why to sacrifice virgins or rip humans hearts for the same bonus?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878375#post878375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's even a legacy for that, though I think the ruling arcana is Time instead of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not remember them - could you point me to this Legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-30-2016, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:45:25-07:00","id":878486,"title":"","content":"Which Arcana is best serve by mutilating your own flesh as a Yantra?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:51:49-07:00","id":878500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878486#post878486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Arcana is best serve by mutilating your own flesh as a Yantra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually Life. Like a Whipping Boy for example. A BESM legacy. Not only is it a yantra for them but an oblation. So they get bonus dice and mana if they take an hour to do a spell. In combat obviously they would try to cut themselves or similar for the dice bonus. <br /> <br /> They remind me of some types of Dreamspeakers and Verbena in MtAsc. The nasty powerful types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 04-30-2016, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:56:00-07:00","id":878508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878388#post878388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_Break_(2015_film)#Plot&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_...015_film)#Plot</a><br /> <br /> <br /> I went and saw this movie after the Mysterium discussions we had on this forum. I hoped it would help me think about them. /shrug<br /> <br /> Sure. I'm not saying my suggestion is finely honed or anything, especially before seeing the final rules. I'm just throwing out an idea for others to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you are trying to go for but honestly if I'm going to go extreme I'd just go full left hand path or worse. Better bang for the buck in my opinion.<br /> <br /> It's why praxis and inured spells along with rotes are seriously advantageous in 2e. You can have as many praxis spells as you want by the way. Also I'd assume any mage that can make rotes would do so and possibly put curses or requirements into them if they have the time. If for nothing else as trading chips.<br /> <br /> I mean why not make a rote with a basic result for outsiders with other levels unlockable depending if you're in her order, path or legacy? Or bad stuff for mages, orders, legacies, paths you don't like. That was in the ToM and was supposed to be the advanced rules for magic. Or more exactly the complete rules.<br /> <br /> You would want to be very careful with the latter option but it's totally possible to do given it's a rote you created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 04-30-2016, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:05:26-07:00","id":878515,"title":"","content":"I would think the first thing you gain from human sacrifice is mana, 1ED let you harvest so much if you were the one to strike the killing blow. Besides Reach perhaps such a Yantra would provide free mana that could be used for additional gain. The obvious might be escaping Paradox, but some spells or added effects require the expenditure of mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:31:50-07:00","id":878529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878515#post878515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think the first thing you gain from human sacrifice is mana, 1ED let you harvest so much if you were the one to strike the killing blow. Besides Reach perhaps such a Yantra would provide free mana that could be used for additional gain. The obvious might be escaping Paradox, but some spells or added effects require the expenditure of mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Seriously you have to know pattern scouring and blood sacrifice will be in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:46:04-07:00","id":878538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878508#post878508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand what you are trying to go for but honestly if I'm going to go extreme I'd just go full left hand path or worse. Better bang for the buck in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you understand at all what I was saying. I thought the word &quot;extreme&quot; was a reference to &quot;extreme sports&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:49:50-07:00","id":878543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878538#post878538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you understand at all what I was saying. I thought the word &amp;quot;extreme&amp;quot; was a reference to &amp;quot;extreme sports&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't directed at you but Wyrdhamster, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T01:53:18-07:00","id":878612,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's Wise (hah) to manipulate these dice bonuses without the context. I feel that these +5 dark yantras would throw a spanner into design of spellcasting, as it apparently is balanced about +3 being hard to get, with +1 being the bread and butter. If you really wanted to make it attractive, how about allowing to use mana gained in the sacrifice &quot;in one go&quot;, bypassing mana-per-turn rules to boost the spell? This way it serves as a shortcut to power, which is usually what black magic is about.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Basically, imagine you have 10 mana and human sacrifice worth 5 mana. You do the ritual, do the sacrifice as the last yantra; it should give you 5 mana, but you already are full; instead of being wasted, it goes towards your spell. Then you apply 10 of your own mana to make a powerful spell that uses a lot of Reach.<br /> I guess you could do this anyway by bleeding mana into the ritual per turn and regaining it by doing sacrificies as yantras (so you empty out your mana tank, but refill it during yantras). No need for extra dice, it seems practical enough. You don't get to cast &quot;theoretically more powerfull spells&quot; than anyone else, as your maximum is the same, but you get to cast at your peak easier and you can replenish your resources easier, so you get to cast at your peak easier even more. With Dark Magic, you can afford using the juice. If you increase yantra bonus per sacrifice to +5 (which is possibly what is in the book anyway, because I remember someone somewhere mumbling that yantra bonus for sacrifice might be equal to mana gained), you will bloat dark spells numerically by a lot; imagine that it gives you 5 dot yantra and that you are sacrificing 3 people, so you get +15 to your spell roll (though you need to spend 10 on spell factors). That's oppressively too much. And before you go &quot;but a willpower adds +3!&quot;, well...maybe the system was balanced while calculating that in?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-30-2016, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T05:14:20-07:00","id":878669,"title":"","content":"To be clear - I'm not sticking still to Yantra ;arger bonus idea because it's mine - I just see problems with other takes shown till this moment. If you have cool idea on making Left Hand practices more profitable to characters - post them still, we will talk them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878612#post878612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's Wise (hah) to manipulate these dice bonuses without the context. I feel that these +5 dark yantras would throw a spanner into design of spellcasting, as it apparently is balanced about +3 being hard to get, with +1 being the bread and butter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great joke! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We need to make some urgings to use such dramatic occult practices - I'm still open to alternatives, but for me, minor mechanics break on easier spellcasting is worthy of Wisdom sin actions. If I ( or my players ) could get the same results with non-Left Hand Yantras, they would use them, instead of trying dark path that will doom they character - don't you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878612#post878612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really wanted to make it attractive, how about allowing to use mana gained in the sacrifice &quot;in one go&quot;, bypassing mana-per-turn rules to boost the spell? This way it serves as a shortcut to power, which is usually what black magic is about.<br /> <br /> (And rest of Mana tricks proposed)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one problem with take on Mana - at least in 1E, I do not remember single spell that needed more than 5 Mana to cast surely. Even then, Gnosis 5 characters ( middle-tier play, attainable by players ) can in rules get the same results in one turn. The same rules are in <b>Werewolf</b> 2E for Primal Urge and Essence as I check my copy. And characters with one middle size Hallow 3+ and access to Legacy Oblations just forget about Mana problems in mass opponents situations.<br /> <br /> Of course, in <b>Mage</b> 2E those factors could have changed with mechanics shifts, but they still be dubious to get &quot;fast Mana burning&quot; bonus - most of Left Hand Yantras you do not make inside combat situation where Mana limits can be factors. To use those bonuses, you look for the victim, make proper circumstances and only then reaping the effects with Wisdom sin roll on you. To get all this length only to get faster Mana burning on spells that do not need them as much I do not see as very convincing for future Mad and Scelesti.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T05:40:00-07:00","id":878675,"title":"","content":"You spend Mana to reduce paradox. You get paradox by Reaching to make your spell more powerful. If you can spend more mana at once, you can cast more powerful spells without them blowing in your face.<br /> Problem with making Left Handed path objectively more powerful is that it will make it objectively more powerful, which isn't really the default stance the game takes on it. Kinda like Dark Side - Left Handed Path is supposed to be quicker, easier, more dangerous, but not more powerful. And, from practical stand point, if you make Left Handed practices too good, you will invite an arms race where you either use left handed means or are left behind in dust. It's healthier for the game to not make non-desirable (and left handed practices are such; after all, default protagonists are not supposed to follow left handed path) options too good, because it's a no win situation - PCs are punished if they follow the spirit of the game and don't use them, and they are punished if they do use them.<br /> Actually, I think that the basic problem here is that game doesn't really want you to consider going Left-Handed, while you want game to want you to go Left-Handed. Kinda like many Star Wars games don't encourage going Dark Side in default rules, and open that up only in &quot;antagonist sourcebooks&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for mana problems - I think that having basically unlimited mana as long as you can sacrifice something, someone, is a great perk to have. It won't make you more powerful in *a single instance*, but it's a broad power boost. Dark Side doesn't need nukes, not being bound by constraints and limits is good enough on it's own (and doesn't make non left handers losers).<br /> <br /> As for Gnosis 5 - people really consider that mid tier gnosis? It always seemed like end-game Gnosis for us, with &quot;middle of the road&quot; being 3 at most...<br /> <br /> Also, you missed something -even if you can spend 5 mana per turn, if you are doing a ritual, you will only pour 10 mana into it (or whatever is your mana limit); doing a human sacrifice as a part of ritual will restore ~5 mana points instantly, so you &quot;cheated in&quot; another 5 mana points into the ritual, exceeding your basic limit. That's 5 paradox dice removed from the roll, increasing your paradox reduction by half (10 --&gt; 15). That's a reach or two. This, curiously, works better if your gnosis is lower, because you get less paradox per reach, while mana remains constant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-30-2016, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:07:03-07:00","id":878736,"title":"","content":"After some extra thinking, I really like potential relationship between Gnosis and Sacrifices. Early on, when every Reach gives you small Paradox pool, that unholy burst of Mana is enough to get you high and more; one sacrifice is all you need, and you are swimming in energy. But as your Gnosis rises, Paradox per Reach gets bigger, and your usual sacrifices start being less and less efficient; this, coupled with the lifestyle you estabilished and standards you adopted, this becomes very annoying, so you try to make it right. And best way to do it is by sacrificing more people.<br /> This is, by the way, a very basic technique that pyramid schemes and cults (and Seers of the Throne, probably) use to strengthen their grip on their victims - they introduce them to desirable lifestyle (money, partners, food, free stuff, social respect), let them adopt it as their default state, and then they pose a danger to it or take it away - most of the time, people won't feel good about downgrading their lifestyle, so they will work extra hard to get it back. <br /> Kind of like you could comfortably live without a cell phone today, or with your old model; but after you switch to new one, and it breaks after you got accustomed to it, it doesn't feel *right* to use the old one, you feel pressure to buy one with all the gadgets the broken one had, right?<br /> Well, human sacrifices do that to you :V.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T09:54:41-07:00","id":878822,"title":"","content":"Sacrifices can already be used as Yantras, for a bonus equal to the amount of Mana otherwise gained. Under 1.5e rules, that's anywhere from +6 to +10, usually +7.<br /> <br /> If the ST allow a suitably specific sacrifice (like, say, a virgin) to count as another Yantra, that's another +2. So +8 to +12 in 2 Yantras, or +4 to +6 per Yantra.<br /> <br /> Is there a way to make sacrifices go off Integrity instead of health (don't think historical sacrifices were usually the more innocent, more often the more expendable)? We'll see in the corebook. Or in Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T10:21:38-07:00","id":878839,"title":"","content":"Time to make a Time Guardian with a &quot;Human Sacrifice&quot; as their Mask-Sin, sacrifice people to fuel prepared spells, and then Shifting Sands to scene before they got sacrificed, with spell already cast :V.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T10:38:12-07:00","id":878855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878822#post878822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sacrifices can already be used as Yantras, for a bonus equal to the amount of Mana otherwise gained. Under 1.5e rules, that's anywhere from +6 to +10, usually +7.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were are those? I do not remember them from GMC Stop Gap topic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T13:48:18-07:00","id":878981,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's in the Yantras spoiler?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T14:18:18-07:00","id":879003,"title":"","content":"No, I think somewhere asked Dave a question how to run Blood Sacrifice in 1.5, and he suggested doing the above for the stopgap solution. It could be on other forums, or maybe here, but I have 4chan &quot;ask me anything&quot; kicking my memory's door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T00:02:41-07:00","id":879335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878855#post878855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were are those? I do not remember them from GMC Stop Gap topic...</div> </div> </div> </div>Until 2e core comes out and says otherwise (or the same, for that matter), Mage core 1e p.78 is the source:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages don\u2019t like to talk about it, but there is an unsavory practice that can also yield up Mana to a mage: the blood sacrifice of a living creature. Animals of cat-size or larger (Size 2 or more) provide one Mana each, although only one such killing per day provides Mana. A human provides one Mana per Health point (an already-wounded victim has less Mana to yield than a healthy one), but the victim must die; he cannot be bled until he is close to death. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T06:55:06-07:00","id":879496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/878180-2e-left-hand-yantras?p=878463#post878463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not remember them - could you point me to this Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Left Hand Path, but I don't remember the page number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:23:15-07:00","id":882231,"title":"","content":"So, officially, human sacrifices can only pay your Mana limits. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAW 2E, p.87</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Sacrifice offers Mana. In an Act of Hubris, the mage kills a living being for Mana. Its death releases Mana from its Pattern. A small animal offers one Mana, while human sacrifices offer as much Mana as the person had Integrity dots remaining before the killing blow. The Mana gained from Sacrifice ignores the spend/Turn limits on Mana if the sacrifice is part of a spell\u2019s casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned in previous posts - I think it's not enough were Mana limits are not so important. Until I find contrary, I will use my &quot;Extreme&quot; Yantra idea. Will see more deeply for the working it with the Rules As Written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T23:52:18-07:00","id":882619,"title":"","content":"Other use for Left Hand magic stuff...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAW 2E, p.98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Destroying a soul is a universally-applicable sacrament Yantra for a Death, Fate, Mind, Prime, or Spirit spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:57:17-07:00","id":882746,"title":"","content":"Mana limists not important? Killing someone allows you to refill tons of your HP bar, for example (awesome for Magical &quot;Vampires&quot;, by the way). And it helps you get tons of Reach. If you give them obscenely high Yantra Values, Left Handed Mages are going to cast Potency 10+ Rituals without problems, and you won't be able to fight back without doing it yourself. It really escalates arms race to the point where it warps the basic stance of the game on the matter. I mean, if you want to give them extra powers, give them Creative Reach Options so they can use extra mana to pay for them, instead of skyrocketing the Dice Pool. A Gnosis 3 Mage with 3 Arcanum who Sacrifices 3 people with Integrity 5 is going to get 3+3+3+5+5+5 dice pool, AND about 7 Free Reaches from Mana Alone! That's 24 Dice Pool, which translates to about 9 safe Spell Factors increases. You can see where this is going?<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> I'm dumb. That would be 29 Dice Pool, because why not just go and take extra casting time? That, of course, increases Safe Spell Factors by another 2, to 11. Do you like Potency +10 potency spells that can last for months, and that can be cast any time you kidnap 3 hobos?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-05-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T03:47:13-07:00","id":949963,"title":"","content":"Newest <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sheer-perfection-signs-of-sorcery-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Perfected Materials</b> blog post</a> and it's Organic Materials section made half of Hack unneeded. I do not know what to think, but generally like proposed ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T12:24:23-07:00","id":950686,"title":"","content":"A non yantra related thought I had about the subject involves permanent durations. If you want a spell to last indefinitely without sacrificing a piece of your own will to maintain it (willpower dot), just sacrifice a sentient and bind their soul to the spell, forcing their 'ghost' to maintain its integrity for you the way they once unconsciously maintained their heart beat. It would provide a mechanical benefit, fit with ancient traditions of burying a sacrifice under new buildings and add an element of haunting to ancient magical works, even if its limited to magi studying it with focused sight seeing the echoes of a soul crying out for release.<br /> \u200bIt would be a very 'Reaper' thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:15:31-07:00","id":950806,"title":"","content":"My GM asked for something that would be &quot;equal&quot; to mechanical terms to Willpower sacrifice when safely freeing a spell. After some thinking, I arrived at idea that you could sacrifice Soul Stones to do so instead - as they, too, demand Willpower sacrifice to create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:21:12-07:00","id":950903,"title":"","content":"Would that be the end of the Soul Stone? Would it still offer the value of a Demesne?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:00:55-07:00","id":951226,"title":"","content":"I think about making Human Blood as universal Yantra +2 - yours is easier to get, easily, but it gives you Bashing damage or Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:05:15-07:00","id":951229,"title":"","content":"It should only be +1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:10:04-07:00","id":951233,"title":"","content":"The idea is that it leads to difficulties for you ( Bashings or Condition ) - or Wisdom breaches when taken from others. Clearly it leads it to 'more difficult to get' category, i.e. typical +2 bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:17:26-07:00","id":951235,"title":"","content":"I could argue for +2 if used in a spell targeting the donor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:18:22-07:00","id":951237,"title":"","content":"I guess a resistant Lethal wound could give you a +2 sacrament.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:24:57-07:00","id":951243,"title":"","content":"That would be a more appropriate drawback, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:23:27-07:00","id":951270,"title":"","content":"Maybe the act of using blood makes lethal wound that created it Resistant and counts against the number of Pattern Frayings you can do in a day, similar to Devouring the Slain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:30:07-07:00","id":951531,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>, good call here. Yeah 1 Resistant Lethal sounds fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T03:18:11-07:00","id":951578,"title":"","content":"Thing about +2 Yantra is that it should provide some real kind of drawback to the user - like a drug related condition, for example. The problem with wounds is that bashing wounds disappear very quickly, and yantras lose their power when condition attached to them lapses; so it seem semi-logical that in order to fortify the blood yantra to 2, you need to fortify the wound.<br /> You probably could create a niche Death spell that allows you to waltz around the Fraying limit per day to make necromancers (and possibly life-mancers) better at this kind of stuff. Something similar to Perfected Sacrifices.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Bashing wound isn't really a drawback, as it disappears naturally - resistant or not - in about 15 minutes; what I foresee is people cutting themselves at every non combat occasion to get that sweet +2 yantra rolling and then walking it off. Lethal wound, on the other hand, takes 3 days to heal up, which can provide serious drawback that might or might not be worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-16-2016, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}